# Architecture

## Living atlas

Deep “how it works now” docs (Mermaid, ingest, hosting, stack rationale): **`docs/architecture/`**.  
Keep them in sync per `.cursor/rules/architecture-docs.mdc`.

## Layout

```
/apps
  /app            # Expo universal client (web + iOS + Android)
  /admin          # Vite editorial SPA (internal; ADR-006)
  /api            # .NET 8 Web API — only process that talks to Postgres
/packages
  /shared-types   # TS types generated from API OpenAPI (NSwag)
/infra
  /docker         # Dockerfiles for api and app (web static)
  /migrations     # EF Core migrations (checked in; never edit applied ones)
/docs
  /architecture   # Living system atlas
  /adr            # One markdown file per architecture decision
  PRD.md          # Product requirements — read before structural/product changes
```

## Hard boundaries

- **API is the only thing that talks to the database.** Frontend never queries Postgres/Neon directly.
- **All new endpoints must appear in the OpenAPI document** exposed by the API. Shared TS types are generated from that document.
- **No breaking changes to shared-types without updating API and consumers (Expo app and/or admin) in the same PR.**
- **No auth for MVP readers** (see `docs/adr/002-no-auth-mvp.md`). Admin uses shared password + JWT (`docs/adr/005-admin-shared-credential.md`).
- **One reader client codebase:** Expo in `apps/app` serves web (MVP hosting) and native later. Do not add a separate Vite/CRA **reader**. Admin Vite SPA at `apps/admin` is a narrow exception (`docs/adr/006-internal-admin-spa.md`).
- **Placeholder product name is TazaKhabar** (packages, titles, manifests). Find-and-replace when the real name is chosen — do not invent alternate brand names.
- **MVP UI is light with a single blue accent** (no multi-color brand palette / logo yet) so full branding can land later without a UI rebuild.

## Before structural changes

Read `docs/architecture/` (matching page), `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc`, and `docs/PRD.md`. Prefer an ADR under `docs/adr/` when changing hosting, auth, data ownership, or monorepo shape.
